  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "triads-introduction",
      "title": "Triads — Introduction",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** theory | **Tier:** intro | **Difficulty:** 2/10\n**Prerequisites:** Major Scales — Introduction\n**Tags:** triads, chords"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A **triad** stacks two thirds above a root — the basic harmonic unit of Western and much folk music."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "qualities",
      "title": "Qualities",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "- **Major**: M3 + m3 (C-E-G)\n- **Minor**: m3 + M3 (A-C-E)\n- **Diminished**: m3 + m3 (B-D-F)\n- **Augmented**: M3 + M3 (C-E-G♯)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "roman-numerals-in-major",
      "title": "Roman numerals in major",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "I, ii, iii, IV, V, vi, vii° — capital = major, lowercase = minor, ° = diminished."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "entities": [],
  "entity_order": [],
  "playlist": [],
  "tunes": [],
  "key_points": [],
  "reading_list": [],
  "quiz_markdown": "### Q1. C major triad notes:\n\n- A) C-E-G\n- B) C-E♭-G\n- C) C-F-A\n- D) C-D-G\n\n**Answer:** A\n\n### Q2. Minor triad has smaller third above root than major.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q3. V is major in a major key.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q4. Triad has three distinct pitch classes.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q5. vii° is diminished in major.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q6. Folk accompaniment often uses I, IV, V, vi.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q7. Augmented triad is rare but appears as passing colour.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q8. Root is the note the triad is named after.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q9. ii is minor in major keys.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q10. Triads build from intervals learned previously.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q11. Three notes define chord quality.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q12. Session guitar uses triad shapes in G and D often.\n\n**Answer:** True",
